  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "T02-F1",
      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "text": "Two different admissibility regimes coexist: (a) per-pair 10% rules (reference dominance, output-policy dominance) and (b) two-arm v3 fixed absolute budget B=10 WRMS. B is a pass/fail budget, not a matched-achieved-error comparison; PW06/T09 must not treat equal-rtol or B-pass as matched achieved error."
    },
    {
      "id": "T02-F2",
      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "text": "stored_state_bytes is retained output size, not peak RSS. WorkCounters has no explicit allocation, peak-memory, setup or startup-work field; the handoff requires these to be charged in PW06/T09, so they must be measured outside this ledger or added with owner approval."
    },
    {
      "id": "T02-F3",
      "severity": "INFO",
      "text": "Analytic reference problems carry reference_uncertainty_wrms = 0.0 (offload digest cited adaptive_global_error.rs L343; not independently re-read here); numerical references derive uncertainty only from Richardson + method disagreement."
